1. Elia Stellaria is attending V Expo, the first VTuber convention in England and possibly Europe, where she will host two panels and a meet-and-greet. (Verbatim: "V Expo is the first VTuber convention in England, I think in Europe, like ever. And it's going to be in England, it's going to be in Birmingham, I'm going to be doing two panels and a meet and greet.")

2. She lives in England. (Verbatim: "I live in England, it's grim all the time, so...")

3. She has a strong interest in and frequently plays Teamfight Tactics (TFT), which she describes as consuming and almost like a religion. (Verbatim: "Can I interest you in my religion, teamfight tactics? It will consume you.")

4. She has an addictive personality and tends to become deeply obsessed with games. (Verbatim: "I have a very addictive personality. Like, very, very, very.")

5. She is stubborn and has difficulty quitting games, even when tired or in a losing streak, due to her aversion to feeling like she has lost. (Verbatim: "I'm stubborn. You guys have seen, I'm like, I'm like a very, very stubborn person... I can't, I can't lose.")

6. She previously played the visual novel Danganronpa for over 20 hours straight without sleeping, driven by the need to know what happens next. (Verbatim: "I ended up playing... Danganronpa like non-hecking stop... I need to find out what happens. I need sleep, but I need to find out what happens more.")

7. She played the visual novel 999 (Nine Hours, Nine Persons, Nine Doors) around 2014 or 2015, several years after its 2009 release. (Verbatim: "I wanna say I played it in 2014, 2015 or something.")

8. She has been accepted into the beta for the game *Tribe 9*, developed by the creator of *Danganronpa* and *999*. (Verbatim: "I got into the beta for it... Tribe 9, I have, I got into the beta for it.")

9. She enjoys games with multiple endings and puzzle elements, such as *999* and *Danganronpa*. (Verbatim: "It was one of those of like, all the multiple different endings, and people just kept stabbing me in the back...")

10. She has previously participated in a panel at Off-Kai, another convention. (Verbatim: "Well, we had a panel at Off-Kai, I think. Yeah, it was Off-Kai, right?") [end of text]



1. She initially pursued medicine but dropped out before starting because she lacked motivation to help people in that capacity. (Verbatim: "i dropped out before before the first before i even started because i just knew i just knew i was like this is gonna be so much effort")

2. She shifted from medicine to a science-related field, then moved into computer science during her master's degree. (Verbatim: "then i went down like scientist kind of route um which then turned into more computer science um when i went to do my master's")

3. She was planning to pursue a doctorate based on her master's thesis but ultimately decided against it. (Verbatim: "then i was going to go to do my doctorate to continue the work my master's thesis was in")

4. Her parents were strongly focused on her securing a stable, prestigious job and were proud of the prospect of her becoming a "doctor," even if not medical. (Verbatim: "my parents were like yo she might not be medical doctor but she can still become doctor exciting right yes yes our hopes and dreams are in this child")

5. She decided to become a VTuber instead of pursuing a PhD after realizing she lacked passion for academia, unlike her peers. (Verbatim: "i want to become a vtuber because like that's that's what i want to do and here i am yay")

6. A key factor in her decision to leave academia was a professor telling her not to do a PhD just for the title, which was her main motivation. (Verbatim: "don't do a doctor if you just want the doctor title and i was like to be honest that is literally my sole reason")

7. She values passion in work and believes those with passion will always surpass those without, which influenced her leaving the PhD path. (Verbatim: "people with passion will always always overtake um for sure")

8. She previously worked in data entry, which she initially found fun by treating it like a game to achieve high speeds. (Verbatim: "i did like data entry for a bit super easy super i found it fun for a bit until the novelty wore off but i was just having fun trying to like give myself a new high score")

9. She was once employed at a company where the head could barely use a computer, which frustrated her. (Verbatim: "i remember one company i worked for the head of it couldn't use a computer i was like why is this punk the head of it getting paid more than double everyone else here")

10. During college, she skipped many classes but was not expelled because the school needed her high grades. (Verbatim: "technically based on my attendance i should have been expelled because i wasn't there half the time... we need your grades like the the school needs your grades so they couldn't kick me out") [end of text]



1. She earned a bachelor's degree in animal biology and a master's in computer science. (Verbatim: "my bachelor's was like um animal biology and then my master's was computer science")

2. She has worked multiple IT jobs simultaneously, often up to three at a time, to support family finances. (Verbatim: "i think yeah most of the time would be like three jobs at a time so i've done like first second third line support")

3. She is a fully trained data scientist and lab scientist. (Verbatim: "i am a fully trained data scientist i'm also a fully trained lab scientist")

4. She dislikes database architecture (DBA) work, describing it as painful and poorly managed. (Verbatim: "i really dislike dba work there's never the right schema for the day i had to organize a full database re-architecture and it hurt it hurt")

5. She finds SQL (or "sequel") easy to learn and recommends it as a simple skill to add to a resume. (Verbatim: "sequel is really nice to pick up it's really easy to pick up and yeah sequel... it's super easy to pick up")

6. She struggled with attending college classes despite perfect grades, leading to administrative conflict. (Verbatim: "the classes i wasn't going to i was getting a hundred percent... so if i just keep getting a hundred percent i don't have to go and they were like yeah you're right")

7. She believes her spoken demeanor doesn't reflect her intelligence, noting people are often surprised by her academic performance. (Verbatim: "i don't give off the vibe of a very smart person and when people would find out about my grades they'd be like huh")

8. She identifies emotionally with cats, saying she was "basically raised by my cat" and often jokes about being a cat. (Verbatim: "i'm almost convinced i'm not a goose i'm a cat i was basically raised by my cat")

9. She suffers from chronic self-doubt, anxiety, and negative thinking despite appearing positive to others. (Verbatim: "i know i come across as a positive person i'm not i'm a very negative person... got a head full of self-doubt all the time")

10. She is extremely ambitious and wants to make a big difference in the world. (Verbatim: "i am extremely ambitious and yeah i want to be able to make a big big big difference like big difference in the world") [end of text]



1. She had a cat that was very attached to her, often sitting on her head while she lay on her side. (Verbatim: "my cat would just sit there... just sit on my head like that and that was that was one of the spots my cat liked to just sit")  
2. Her cat followed her to every room, though it didn’t always sit close—just stayed within view. (Verbatim: "if i moved to another room my cat would just follow me and wouldn't sit with me but like sit like in view of me")  
3. The cat was affectionate only with her, especially at night, and would knead ("make biscuits") and purr while near her. (Verbatim: "always purr always always always purr with me... making biscuits kneading bread like the yum yum yum yum")  
4. The cat was standoffish with others and not friendly toward people outside the household. (Verbatim: "this cat was not friendly with other people... it was a very standoffish cat")  
5. She misses her cat deeply and has a strong affection for cats in general. (Verbatim: "i miss my cat i miss my cat i love cats")  
6. She previously overworked herself during university, neglecting sleep and food in favor of work. (Verbatim: "i'm like i don't need sleep or to look after myself i don't need food i need time to work to work to work")  
7. She believes self-care is important and recognizes she can’t perform at her best without taking care of herself. (Verbatim: "can't do my best if i'm not at my best")  
8. She is British, as indicated by her accent and self-reference. (Verbatim: "remember i'm british so i'm gonna have to give it")  
9. She wants to do a karaoke stream in the future. (Verbatim: "what i really need to do a karaoke stream i really need to do a karaoke stream one day")  
10. She has a habit of needing post-stream downtime to mentally decompress after broadcasting. (Verbatim: "after every stream i need to have like a... cool down i guess like post stream just down time") [end of text]



1. She previously worked at a zoo, which involved physically demanding tasks like lifting heavy bags of food and hay. (Verbatim: "one of the things they don't tell you... when you work at the zoo there's a lot of lifting like those... food pellets those are like 30 kilo bags... it sucks like yeah having to carry a 30 kilo food bag...")

2. She has experience working with a variety of animals, including rhinos, zebras, donkeys, cows, and birds, and learned their individual personalities. (Verbatim: "working with all the different animals and learning all their different personalities... each one had such a personality to them and it was really sweet")

3. She specifically cared for two rhinos, one calm and one frequently aggressive, which required adjusting their living arrangements based on mood. (Verbatim: "there were two rhinos i looked after one was really gentle... the other one woke up and decided to choose violence every two or three days")

4. She had to care for hand-reared animals, including a cow that would run away from inexperienced handlers, requiring assertiveness to control. (Verbatim: "there was one cow that was hand-reared... every time someone new joined it would be their first task to walk this one hecking cow and this cow knew")

5. She worked in falconry and cared for birds such as a falcon, Harris hawks, a snowy white owl, and the Eurasian eagle owl, though she wasn’t trained to fly the latter due to its dangerous strength. (Verbatim: "i also had to look after a bunch of birds... there's the falcon obviously... the eurasian eagle owl but i didn't actually get to fly the eurasian eagle owl because... the claws... are strong enough to crush your skull")

6. She struggled with being assertive, especially during falconry, due to her British manner of speaking politely rather than commandingly. (Verbatim: "i always sucked at that... i'm british right i'm gonna be like yo bird would you like to come over... and they're like no you need to say it with dominance")

7. She prefers cardio exercises over weight training and enjoys using the cross trainer and rowing machine. (Verbatim: "i like cardio cardio my beloved cross trainer my beloved rowing machine my beloved all the basic stuff")

8. She dislikes core workouts because they cause pain that affects daily activities like laughing and walking. (Verbatim: "i struggle most with core... when you exercise your core and then it like hurts to laugh and and that sucks")

9. She does not mind leg day workouts and finds them easier to recover from compared to core exercises. (Verbatim: "i don't mind leg day that much guys... if you've done leg day it's fine like i it's very easy to let my legs rest")

10. She identifies as British and often references her British background, including using British units (kilos) and humor. (Verbatim: "remember i'm british so i'm gonna have to give it in kilos because goodness knows how how hacking units work") [end of text]



1. She has a medically diagnosed history of agoraphobia and has undergone therapy for it. (Verbatim: "i had agoraphobia um like proper like you know proper medically diagnosed got given therapy for in all sorts um yeah")

2. She finds crowds and gatherings of people difficult and instinctively avoids routes with many people. (Verbatim: "i'm scared of people but i can cope and i can outweigh you know oh i do want to go to said event even if there are people there")

3. She used to take long walks with her dog, but learned the hard way that she must plan looped routes to avoid exhausting return trips without fast travel. (Verbatim: "i did this ridiculously long hike and i was so far away from home and it started raining and i was so sad... i have to walk all the way back why is there no fast travel")

